          "channel": "other",
          "instructions": "Bank-side freeze per the bank's UPI page 'Block UPI Transactions' section: 'Customers can send an SMS with keyword BLOCKUPI to number 9895088888 or 5676762 to block UPI transactions in their federal bank account. Upon receipt of the SMS, bank will block UPI in all eligible accounts linked to the mobile number from which SMS is received'; a Success/Failure response SMS is sent back to the same number. In-app deregistration (FedMobile): 'Go to the ‘UPI Payments’ option > Click on ‘View Profile’ > Click on ‘De-register’'; caveat: 'Once the UPI ID is de-registered the same UPI ID cannot be retrieved or re-used for a period of 2 years from the de-registration date', and uninstalling an app doesn't delete profile data 'and hence can lead to misuse at the later point in time'. Lost device with UPI Lite: 'Please contact us immediately to get your UPI Lite balance refunded to your account.' Report unauthorized UPI transactions via the bank's portal https://portal.federal.bank.in/unauth_txns/ (linked from the UPI page) or the NPCI Dispute Redressal portal (npci.org.in/what-we-do/upi/dispute-redressal-mechanism). Contact Centre (UPI page header tel: links + Contact Center page: 'Dial the pan India toll free number 1800 - 425 - 1199 Or 1800 - 420 - 1199'); from abroad 0484-2630994 / 0484-2630995 / 080-61991199, 24x7. Official download link for the bank's UPI app (FedMobile): 'Link to Download our UPI App' -> https://fedmobile.federalbank.co.in/download/ ('Available on Google Playstore & iOS'; direct Play/App Store URLs not published on the fetched pages and the FedMobile microsite host was unreachable at verification time, so androidApp/iosApp keys are omitted). No netbanking (FedNet) UPI manage path published (FedNet page bot-blocked at verification), and the bank's SMS-banking page lists no UPI keyword (only debit BLOCK and credit FBCCBLOCK), so BLOCKUPI comes from the UPI page alone.",
